{"id":"kolu-held-needs-quiet","parent":"kolu-root","ord":"a4","title":"PR: kolu's Claude Code sensor reports running_background while async subagents run #upstream","todo":true,"desc":"**TL;DR.** Kolu's Claude Code sensor reports a main agent as `waiting` while its async subagents still run, so olai's terminal doorbell rings \"idle\" on a busy terminal. Kolu already has the right state (`running_background`) and an open fix (PR #2171 for issue #2140, stale against master). This item lands that fix. Not dispatched; awaiting the human's word.\n\n**What was seen (2026-09-03, #486's author terminal 3c6db249).** Claude Code had ended its main turn and was waiting on seven of its own background subagents. Kolu reported the terminal's agent state as `waiting`. olai-plugin-kolu's doorbell, which folds that state through kolu's `agentBucket`, said \"it has finished, or it needs you\". The Dock's activity spinner, which reads output bytes, was still turning.\n\n**How kolu decides a state is held.** `packages/padi/src/attention/stateWatch.ts` and the padi README, section on `--held-for`: the level is `agentBucket(agent.state)`, the state the agent's own adapter published. Output bytes are deliberately not read. The reason is recorded there: a quiet screen is not an idle agent (an idle grok repaints once a second, which starved a byte-quiet gate in #2177), and a busy screen is not a busy agent. So \"hold the clock while output flows\" would reverse a documented kolu decision. It is not the fix.\n\n**The state that already exists for this case.** Kolu's vocabulary has `running_background`: the agent ended its turn while background work of its own is still running. `agentBucket` folds it into `working`, so a terminal in that state is never held and never rings. The Claude Code sensor (`packages/integrations/claude-code/src/core.ts`, around line 533) promotes `waiting` to `running_background` only for subagents tagged `fork` with a fresh streaming transcript. Async `Agent` and `Task` subagents write the same artifacts with a different or absent tag, so they are not promoted and the main reads as `waiting`.\n\n**Upstream already knows.** kolu issue #2140 names this exact gap. PR #2171 (opened 2026-08-20, not merged) promotes any subagent with a fresh transcript anchor regardless of tag. As of 2026-09-03 it has no reviews, three comments, and master is 43 commits ahead of it; a sleeping terminal (ef6d1c6b) still holds its worktree.\n\n**What this item is.** Land the #2140 fix: bring #2171 current with master (a merge commit) and take it through kolu's process, or re-cut it on master if the branch has rotted. Done means: a Claude Code main idle under a running async `Agent` or `Task` reads `running_background` in `kolu ls`, the Dock, `kolu wait`, and the olai doorbell; the phantom-safety rule from #2171 (a dead subagent ages out by its stale transcript, a launch marker alone promotes nothing) holds with a test.\n\n**Nothing changes in olai-plugin-kolu.** Its `heldStateOf` (`packages/plugins/kolu/src/client/watch.ts`) reads the published state through kolu's own fold; once the sensor publishes `running_background` the doorbell stops ringing on this case by itself.\n\nFiled 2026-09-03 from the human's observation; first written as an output-activity fix and corrected the same morning after reading kolu's source.","created":"2026-09-03T09:20:17-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T09:24:13-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-09-03 ~09:25 ET, watching the Dock spin under a doorbell that said idle","repo":"repo-kolu"}}
